bigraph -- create a bigraph
***************************

  * Usage: 
        G= bigraph(H)
        G= bigraph(L)
        G= bigraph(V,L)
        G= bigraph(V,A)
        G= bigraph(A)
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, hashtable of edges
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of edges
      * V, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of vertices
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, adjacency matrix 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note EntryMode: bigraph_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmEntryMode=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value "auto", optional input, accepts 'auto', 'edges', or
        'neighbors'
      * *note Singletons: bigraph_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSingletons=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null, optional input, accepts the list of isolated
        vertices in a bigraph
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note Bigraph: Bigraph,, 

Description
===========

This is a constructor of a simple graph of class *note Bigraph: Bigraph,.  One
can use the same input types as in *note graph: (Graphs)graph,.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = bigraph {{3,4},{1,2},{2,4}}|
|                                    |
|o1 = Bigraph{1 => {2}   }           |
|             2 => {4, 1}            |
|             3 => {4}               |
|             4 => {3, 2}            |
|                                    |
|o1 : Bigraph                        |
+------------------------------------+

