File: StatGraphs.info, Node: children_lpMixedGraph_cmThing_rp, Next: collateVertices, Prev: bigraph_lpMixedGraph_rp, Up: Top

children(MixedGraph,Thing) -- return the children of a vertex of a mixed graph
******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note children: (Graphs)children,
  * Usage: 
        children (G,v)
  * Inputs:
      * G, an instance of the type *note MixedGraph: MixedGraph,, 
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, a vertex of G 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, 

Description
===========

The children of v are the all the vertices u such that v,u is in the directed
edge set of the *note MixedGraph: MixedGraph, G. So the children of a vertex v
are exactly those vertices of the largest digraph component of a  mixed graph
that v points to.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = mixedGraph(graph{{3,1}},digraph {{1,2},{2,3}},bigraph {{3,4},{2,4}})|
|                                                                             |
|o1 = MixedGraph{Bigraph => Bigraph{2 => {4}   }}                             |
|                                   3 => {4}                                  |
|                                   4 => {3, 2}                               |
|                Digraph => Digraph{1 => {2}}                                 |
|                                   2 => {3}                                  |
|                                   3 => {}                                   |
|                Graph => Graph{1 => {3}}                                     |
|                               3 => {1}                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : MixedGraph                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : children (G,1)                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = set {2}                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Set                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : children (G,2)                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = set {3}                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Set                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : children (G,3)                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = set {}                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Set                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

