isLoopless -- check whether a graph contains a loop
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isLoopless(G)
  * Inputs:
      * G, graph of class  *note MixedGraph: MixedGraph,,  *note Graph:
        (Graphs)Graph,,  *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph, or  *note Bigraph:
        Bigraph,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This method checks whether a graph contains a loop.

If the input is a  *note Graph: (Graphs)Graph, or a  *note Bigraph: Bigraph,,
then this is equivalent to *note isSimple: (Graphs)isSimple,.

If the input is a  *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,, then this is equivalent to
checking whether the  *note underlyingGraph: (Graphs)underlyingGraph, *note
isSimple: (Graphs)isSimple,.

If the input is a  *note MixedGraph: MixedGraph,, then this checks whether the
undirected, directed and bidirected subgraphs separately contain loops.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : U = graph{{1,2},{2,3},{3,4}}            |
|                                             |
|o1 = Graph{1 => {2}   }                      |
|           2 => {1, 3}                       |
|           3 => {2, 4}                       |
|           4 => {3}                          |
|                                             |
|o1 : Graph                                   |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = digraph{{2,5}}                      |
|                                             |
|o2 = Digraph{2 => {5}}                       |
|             5 => {}                         |
|                                             |
|o2 : Digraph                                 |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = bigraph{{5,6}}                      |
|                                             |
|o3 = Bigraph{5 => {6}}                       |
|             6 => {5}                        |
|                                             |
|o3 : Bigraph                                 |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G = mixedGraph(U,D,B)                   |
|                                             |
|o4 = MixedGraph{Bigraph => Bigraph{5 => {6}}}|
|                                   6 => {5}  |
|                Digraph => Digraph{2 => {5}} |
|                                   5 => {}   |
|                Graph => Graph{1 => {2}   }  |
|                               2 => {1, 3}   |
|                               3 => {2, 4}   |
|                               4 => {3}      |
|                                             |
|o4 : MixedGraph                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isLoopless G                            |
|                                             |
|o5 = true                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
+---------------------+
|i6 : U = graph{{1,1}}|
|                     |
|o6 = Graph{1 => {1}} |
|                     |
|o6 : Graph           |
+---------------------+
|i7 : isLoopless U    |
|                     |
|o7 = false           |
+---------------------+

Ways to use isLoopless:
=======================

  * "isLoopless(Bigraph)"
  * "isLoopless(Digraph)"
  * "isLoopless(Graph)"
  * "isLoopless(MixedGraph)"

