parents(MixedGraph,Thing) -- return the parents of a vertex of a mixed graph
****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note parents: (Graphs)parents,
  * Usage: 
        parents (G,v)
  * Inputs:
      * G, an instance of the type *note MixedGraph: MixedGraph,, 
      * v, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, a vertex of G 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, 

Description
===========

The parents of v are the all the vertices u such that u,v is in the directed
edge set of the *note MixedGraph: MixedGraph, G. So the parents of a vertex v
are exactly those vertices of the largest digraph component of a mixed graph
that point to v.

